<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FBType Name="logiBUS_AI_MVA" Comment="Composite FB for analog input data in millivolts">
	<Identification Standard="61499-2" Description="Copyright (c) 2026 HR Agrartechnik GmbH  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0&#10;&#10;AnalogInput_hysteresis = 0 switches the change trigger off (use 1 to see every change). TimeDelta = 0 or 16#FFFFFFFF switches the cyclic IND off. With both off the block sends no IND (value only via REQ).&#10;&#10;IN = calibrated voltage at the pin in mV (ADC calibration of the chip from eFuse, attenuation as for logiBUS_AI_ID: ESP32-S3 about 0-2900 mV, ESP32-P4 about 0-3300 mV). Without calibration for the channel (e.g. ESP32-S31 with the current ESP-IDF) INIT fails with STATUS = 'ADC calibration not available'.">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="HR Agrartechnik GmbH" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2026-11-13">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="logiBUS::io::AI">
		<Import declaration="logiBUS::io::AI::logiBUS_AI::Invalid"/>
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<EventInputs>
			<Event Name="INIT" Type="EInit" Comment="Service Initialization">
				<With Var="QI"/>
				<With Var="PARAMS"/>
				<With Var="Input"/>
				<With Var="AnalogInput_hysteresis"/>
				<With Var="TimeDelta"/>
				<With Var="TimeRateLimit"/>
			</Event>
			<Event Name="REQ" Type="Event" Comment="Service Request">
				<With Var="QI"/>
			</Event>
		</EventInputs>
		<EventOutputs>
			<Event Name="INITO" Type="EInit" Comment="Initialization Confirm">
				<With Var="QO"/>
				<With Var="STATUS"/>
			</Event>
		</EventOutputs>
		<InputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QI" Type="BOOL" Comment="Event Input Qualifier"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="PARAMS" Type="STRING" Comment="Service Parameters"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="Input" Type="logiBUS::io::AI::logiBUS_AI_S" Comment="Identify the Input Input_I1..I8" InitialValue="Invalid"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="AnalogInput_hysteresis" Type="DWORD" Comment="IND when the voltage changes by more than this many mV (0 = off)"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="TimeDelta" Type="DWORD" Comment="After How many ms an IND (poll interval, 0 or 16#FFFFFFFF = off)" InitialValue="250"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="TimeRateLimit" Type="DWORD" Comment="Maximum 1 IND in how many ms. (&lt; delta)" InitialValue="100"/>
		</InputVars>
		<OutputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QO" Type="BOOL" Comment="Event Output Qualifier"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="STATUS" Type="STRING" Comment="Service Status"/>
		</OutputVars>
		<Sockets>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="SREQ" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AX" Comment="Service Request" x="-1300" y="1800"/>
		</Sockets>
		<Plugs>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="IN" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AD" Comment="Input data from resource, calibrated voltage at the pin in mV" x="3200" y="1200"/>
		</Plugs>
	</InterfaceList>
	<FBNetwork>
		<FB Name="AI" Type="logiBUS::io::AI::logiBUS_AI_MV" x="1240" y="460">
		</FB>
		<FB Name="E_R_TRIG" Type="iec61499::events::E_R_TRIG" x="-600" y="1800">
		</FB>
		<EventConnections>
			<Connection Source="INIT" Destination="AI.INIT" dx1="1486.67"/>
			<Connection Source="AI.INITO" Destination="INITO" dx1="880"/>
			<Connection Source="AI.IND" Destination="IN.E1" dx1="246.67"/>
			<Connection Source="AI.CNF" Destination="IN.E1" dx1="246.67"/>
			<Connection Source="REQ" Destination="AI.REQ" dx1="1453.33"/>
			<Connection Source="E_R_TRIG.EO" Destination="AI.REQ" dx1="246.67"/>
			<Connection Source="SREQ.E1" Destination="E_R_TRIG.EI"/>
		</EventConnections>
		<DataConnections>
			<Connection Source="AI.IN" Destination="IN.D1" dx1="213.33"/>
			<Connection Source="QI" Destination="AI.QI" dx1="1420"/>
			<Connection Source="PARAMS" Destination="AI.PARAMS" dx1="1386.67"/>
			<Connection Source="AI.QO" Destination="QO" dx1="1200"/>
			<Connection Source="AI.STATUS" Destination="STATUS" dx1="1593.33"/>
			<Connection Source="Input" Destination="AI.Input" dx1="1353.33"/>
			<Connection Source="AnalogInput_hysteresis" Destination="AI.AnalogInput_hysteresis" dx1="1320"/>
			<Connection Source="SREQ.D1" Destination="E_R_TRIG.QI"/>
			<Connection Source="TimeDelta" Destination="AI.TimeDelta" dx1="1180"/>
			<Connection Source="TimeRateLimit" Destination="AI.TimeRateLimit" dx1="1060"/>
		</DataConnections>
	</FBNetwork>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>logiBUS_AI_MVA</h1>

<h2>🇩🇪 Deutsch</h2>

<p>Composite-Baustein um <code>logiBUS_AI_MV</code> mit Adapter-Ausgang: <code>IN</code> (Adapter <code>AD</code>) liefert die kalibrierte Spannung am Pin in Millivolt.</p>

<h3>Schnittstelle</h3>

<ul>
	<li><strong>INIT</strong> (mit QI, PARAMS, Input, AnalogInput_hysteresis, TimeDelta, TimeRateLimit): wie <code>logiBUS_AI_MV</code>, wird direkt durchgereicht.</li>
	<li><strong>REQ</strong> (mit QI): sofortige Abfrage; kann zusätzlich über den Socket <code>SREQ</code> extern ausgelöst werden.</li>
	<li><strong>INITO</strong> (mit QO, STATUS): Bestätigung der Initialisierung.</li>
	<li><strong>Plug IN</strong> (<code>adapter::types::unidirectional::AD</code>): liefert die Spannung in mV als Adapter-Ereignis/-Daten (<code>E1</code>/<code>D1</code>) statt der einzelnen <code>CNF</code>/<code>IND</code>-Events des inneren Bausteins.</li>
	<li><strong>Socket SREQ</strong> (<code>adapter::types::unidirectional::AX</code>): externe Service-Anforderung, über <code>E_R_TRIG</code> flankengetriggert auf <code>AI.REQ</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Wert von IN</h3>

<p><code>IN</code> ist die Spannung am Pin des Chips in <strong>Millivolt</strong> (<code>DWORD</code>). Die Firmware rechnet den gemittelten Rohwert mit der Kalibrierung des Chips um (ESP-IDF <code>adc_cali</code>, Werte aus dem eFuse). Die Dämpfung ist dieselbe wie bei <code>logiBUS_AI_ID</code>: ESP32-S3 etwa 0-2900 mV (±50 mV), ESP32-P4 etwa 0-3300 mV (±15 mV), laut Datenblatt.</p>

<p>Die Spannung an der Klemme hängt vom Spannungsteiler der Platine ab und ist nicht eingerechnet.</p>

<p>Gibt es für den Kanal keine Kalibrierung (z. B. ESP32-S31 mit dem aktuellen ESP-IDF), meldet INIT <code>QO</code> = FALSE und <code>STATUS</code> = <code>ADC calibration not available</code>.</p>

<h3>Hysterese und Zeitsteuerung</h3>

<p>Wie bei <code>logiBUS_AI_ID</code>, aber <code>AnalogInput_hysteresis</code> gilt in mV.</p>

<h2>🇬🇧 English</h2>

<p>Composite block around <code>logiBUS_AI_MV</code> with adapter output: <code>IN</code> (adapter <code>AD</code>) delivers the calibrated voltage at the pin in millivolts.</p>

<h3>Interface</h3>

<ul>
	<li><strong>INIT</strong> (with QI, PARAMS, Input, AnalogInput_hysteresis, TimeDelta, TimeRateLimit): same as <code>logiBUS_AI_MV</code>, passed straight through.</li>
	<li><strong>REQ</strong> (with QI): immediate read; can also be triggered externally via the <code>SREQ</code> socket.</li>
	<li><strong>INITO</strong> (with QO, STATUS): initialization confirmation.</li>
	<li><strong>Plug IN</strong> (<code>adapter::types::unidirectional::AD</code>): delivers the voltage in mV as an adapter event/data pair (<code>E1</code>/<code>D1</code>) instead of the internal block's individual <code>CNF</code>/<code>IND</code> events.</li>
	<li><strong>Socket SREQ</strong> (<code>adapter::types::unidirectional::AX</code>): external service request, edge-triggered onto <code>AI.REQ</code> via <code>E_R_TRIG</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Value of IN</h3>

<p><code>IN</code> is the voltage at the chip pin in <strong>millivolts</strong> (<code>DWORD</code>). The firmware converts the averaged raw value with the chip calibration (ESP-IDF <code>adc_cali</code>, eFuse values). The attenuation is the same as for <code>logiBUS_AI_ID</code>: ESP32-S3 about 0-2900 mV (±50 mV), ESP32-P4 about 0-3300 mV (±15 mV), according to the datasheet.</p>

<p>The voltage at the terminal depends on the voltage divider of the board and is not included.</p>

<p>Without a calibration for the channel (e.g. ESP32-S31 with the current ESP-IDF), INIT returns <code>QO</code> = FALSE and <code>STATUS</code> = <code>ADC calibration not available</code>.</p>

<h3>Hysteresis and timing</h3>

<p>As for <code>logiBUS_AI_ID</code>, but <code>AnalogInput_hysteresis</code> is in mV.</p>
]]></Attribute>
</FBType>
